  <exercise data-content-id="3153a984-698b-4cfd-aa54-9e96713c8c68" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="800">
    <problem>
      <para>A backyard farmer wants to enclose a rectangular space for a new garden within her fenced backyard. She has purchased 80 feet of wire fencing to enclose three sides, and she will use a section of the backyard fence as the fourth side. The function is graphed below. What is the maximum area, in square feet, that can be fenced in?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b339c52d8c7cb9ef2eb25f83ba6b879f45b80fe3"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Enter the maximum area in square feet.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The maximum area is 800 square feet.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.11.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
